<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<odoo noupdate="1">
    <!--
        The parameter is created EMPTY, with its description.

        Two reasons. One: so it exists with a visible name under Settings →
        Technical → System Parameters, instead of requiring the key to be typed
        from memory. Two, the one that matters: so whoever sees it knows **what
        it enables** before filling it in. Today it is a line of free text with
        nothing beside it, and this is not a preference — it is the switch
        between "normal Odoo" and "Odoo that lets itself be shown inside another
        site". The session cookie is NOT touched (see the README): what is given
        up is clickjacking protection, and only for the origins the
        administrator declares here.

        Empty changes nothing: the module installed with no origin loaded is
        indistinguishable from not being installed.

        It carries `noupdate="1"` at the root, and that is not cosmetic: without
        it, every `-u tuqui_embed` would rewrite `value` with the XML's empty
        one and switch the customer's embed off without saying anything.
    -->
    <record id="param_embed_origins" model="ir.config_parameter">
        <field name="key">tuqui.embed_origins</field>
        <field name="value"></field>
    </record>
</odoo>
